  "id": "frequency-modulation",
  "term": "frequency modulation",
  "definition": "Frequency modulation is a modeling approach that represents a cell’s action potential by using a constant-amplitude sine wave whose phase and frequency are varied over time. In this context, it is used as a computationally simpler way to emulate cell and tissue electrical activity, including dynamic behavior and coupling between cells.",
